git clone https://github.com/Aysayas/Lavalust-Template.git my-new-project
cd my-new-project

Then double-click setup-new-project.bat (it copies .env.example to .env,
renames the project everywhere, optionally resets git history, and starts
Docker for you - see setup-new-project.bat's comments for details).

IMPORTANT: the "my-new-project" at the end of the git clone line is what
names your folder. If you leave it off, git names the folder after the repo
itself (e.g. "Lavalust-Template") instead of your project - the setup script
renames things INSIDE the project but does not rename its own folder while
running, so pick the folder name at clone time.
